# Build-context exclusions. docker/Dockerfile copies only named directories, so
# nothing here is load-bearing on its own -- this is the second line of defence,
# for the day someone adds a `COPY . .` in a hurry.
#
# The first four entries are the reason this file exists: the working tree of a
# running node carries the live VEYRS_SECRET_KEY, the live Fernet key and a
# production database dump. An image layer is additive and immutable, so a
# secret copied in once cannot be removed by a later RUN rm -- it ships with the
# image to everyone it is shared with.
#
# The patterns are `**/`-prefixed on purpose. A bare `.env` matches ONLY the
# context root -- docker/.env, which veyrs-docker.sh writes and which carries
# the stack's signing key, Fernet key and admin password, would sail straight
# past it. Found by trying to write the mutation test for this file and
# discovering it could not be made to bite.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.bootstrap-credentials
var/

# Never useful in an image, and `venv/` alone is ~400 MB of host-linked
# binaries that would be uploaded to the daemon on every single build.
venv/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
node_modules/
*.dump
*.sql.gz
